<section>
  <div class="container narrow">
    <h2>Why a program approach works</h2>
    <p>Blood pressure responds quickly to a handful of well-chosen daily practices: the right food, the right amount of salt, deeper sleep, slower breath, regular gentle movement and less chronic stress. A program gives you the structure to put all of these in place at once — which is why most people see meaningful change inside a few weeks.</p>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <ul class="checks">
      <li>Adults with diagnosed hypertension on one or more medications.</li>
      <li>People with borderline or rising blood pressure readings.</li>
      <li>Anyone with a strong family history of hypertension or stroke.</li>
      <li>People with related risks — high cholesterol, central weight, sleep apnea.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you'll learn</h2>
    <ul class="checks">
      <li>The role of whole plants, sodium, potassium and processed foods.</li>
      <li>How to read labels and rebuild your kitchen for low-sodium cooking.</li>
      <li>Daily practices for sleep, breathing and stress that move the dial.</li>
      <li>How to track your own blood pressure honestly and confidently at home.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The arc of the program</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card"><div class="icon">①</div><h3>Foundations</h3><p>Understanding your numbers and the levers that move them.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="icon">②</div><h3>Practice</h3><p>Putting food, sleep, breath and movement in place — one week at a time.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="icon">③</div><h3>Hold</h3><p>Locking in the changes so this is how you live, not what you tried.</p></div>
    </div>

